-# OpenMW multiplayer test harness
+# OpenMW multiplayer (a Lua mod)
 
-- `server/relay.py` — newline-delimited JSON relay (`--mirror` echoes you back as a ghost 300 units east).
-- `server/bot.py` — fake second player walking in a circle.
-- `mod/` — `mp.omwscripts` + `scripts/mp/global.lua`, a global script using `openmw.net`:
-  streams the player's cell/position/yaw 5x/second and shows each remote player as a `com_chest_01`.
+Everything here is a mod. The engine only offers generic pieces: TCP sockets (`openmw.net`), animation head/spine tilt
+(`animation.setHeadPitch`), map markers (`ui.setMapMarkers`) and a main-menu button hook. The networking itself (client,
+server, JSON, internet-address lookup), the relay, parties, trade, chat, avatars and all UI are Lua.
 
-Run: `multiplayer/run-test.sh [path/to/openmw]`, then load a save. Watch `openmw.log` for `[mp]` lines.
-Protocol: one JSON object per line, `{"t":"state","name","cell","pos":[x,y,z],"yaw"}`; the server adds `id`.
+```
+mod/mp.omwscripts        what the mod loads
+mod/scripts/mp/
+  netlib.lua             client + server + JSON + public-address lookup on top of openmw.net sockets
+  relay.lua              the server logic that runs inside the host's game
+  bot.lua                a fake player living inside the relay (for testing the UI with one game)
+  global.lua             the client: sync, avatars, parties, commands, time/weather
+  player.lua             UI: chat, party panel, invites, arrows over players, status line, avatar menu
+  menu.lua               main-menu screen (host/join, port, password, test player) and settings renderers
+  remote.lua             runs on avatars/stand-ins: movement, attacks, head tilt, death pose, reading pose
+  proxies.lua            stand-ins for party members' actors, shared kills, no duplicate NPCs
+  trade.lua, damage.lua  trade window, damage/kill delivery to real actors
+server/                  old standalone Python relay (no password/admin/ping list), bots for it
+test/relay_test.lua      runs the relay logic without the game:  luajit multiplayer/test/relay_test.lua
+run-two.sh               two real instances on one machine (host + joiner)
+```
 
 ## Hosting and joining
-From the main menu's Multiplayer screen choose **Join a server** (address + port) or **Host a game** (port), then start or
-load a character. Hosting runs the relay inside your game (`mod/scripts/mp/relay.lua`, on top of `net.listen`) and you play
-through a loopback connection to it, so any number of players can join you. You are connected to exactly one host at a
-time, and while hosting you cannot join another server; to switch, return to the main menu and load again.
-`server/relay.py` is still there for a dedicated server.
-
-## Testing with two real instances
-`multiplayer/run-two.sh <openmw> <save.omwsave>` starts one instance that hosts and a second that joins it (the "fake second
-player"), each with its own user-data dir, and logs to `$TMPDIR/mp-two/{host,join}.log`. The joiner also fakes attacks,
-jumps and sneaking so the host can check the avatar animations. Note both share `~/.config/openmw` settings.
-
-## How it works
-Every player keeps their **own** world; nothing a group member does changes yours.
-- **Presence:** everyone online appears as a stand-in NPC (look + gear) when you share a cell. Activate one for a menu:
-  invite to party, accept/decline, leave party, **trade**.
-- **Parties (max 3):** shared party chat, health/magicka/fatigue panel, and *proxies*: if a member has an NPC/creature
-  alive that is dead or missing in your world you get a marked copy `Name [Alice's world]` (own record, no script, no AI).
-  Damage you do to it is applied to the owner's real actor, so they can finish their quest. Your world is untouched.
-- **Chat:** Enter or Y opens the input (the game keeps running); Enter sends, Tab switches Global/Party.
-  `/accept [name]`, `/decline [name]`, `/leave`, `/g text`, `/p text`.
-- **Trade:** both inventories are shown (like a merchant's goods). Click to add an item to the deal, right-click adds
-  the whole stack; both players must accept the same revision. Items are recreated from their record id on the receiving
-  side (condition/enchant charge reset; runtime-generated items can't be traded). It is not atomic across a crash.
-
-Test with one client: `run-test.sh [--cheat]` starts the relay, a "Bot" player (auto-accepts party invites and trades,
-owns a scrib that doesn't exist in your world) and OpenMW. `server/owner_bot.py --help` lists bot options.
-
-Combat is two-way: hitting a proxy turns on its AI so it fights you in your world, the owner's real actor takes the damage
-and turns on its owner, and other players' avatars can't be hurt (and hitting one gives no bounty).
-
-Quest safety: a guest hitting a proxy only ever *wounds* the owner's real actor (it never drops below 1 health and
-then stands down), so nobody can kill an NPC another player still needs. The guest's own copy dies in their world.
-Players list: Esc > Options > Scripts > Multiplayer shows everyone online with latency (also `/players`, whisper with
-`/w name text`). The host's clock and the weather in the host's region are shared with joiners.
-Avatars mirror sneaking, jumping, attacks and spell casts (animation only, they never deal damage in your world) and are
-moved with velocity extrapolation at 20 updates/s.
-
-Not done: shared fights where both worlds have the actor alive, container contents,
-weather/time, proxies for actors that are alive-but-unloaded in your world, trade of enchanted/generated items.
+Main menu → **Multiplayer**: choose **Join a server** (address, port, password) or **Host a game** (port, optional
+password), then start or load a character. Hosting starts with your game: the relay runs inside it and you play through a
+loopback connection, so host and joiner share the same client code. You are connected to exactly one host at a time and
+while hosting you cannot join another server; to switch, return to the main menu and load again.
+
+When hosting the game looks up your internet address (one request to `api.ipify.org`) and shows it in chat, in the status
+line and on *Options → Scripts → Multiplayer*, together with your LAN address. Friends outside your network need that address
+and the TCP port forwarded on your router to your computer. Joiners also get a list of servers they joined before.
+
+Safety: protocol version check (both sides must run the same mod), optional password, player limit (default 8), unique
+names (a second "Alice" becomes "Alice (2)"), a message of the day, and a 10 second limit to say who you are.
+
+## Playing together
+Every player keeps their **own** world; nothing a group member does changes yours, except the shared things below.
+- **Presence:** everyone appears as a stand-in NPC (look and gear) when you share a cell, with a green arrow and name that
+  shows through walls, and a marker on the map and minimap. Activate someone for a menu: invite to party, trade, ...
+- **Animation:** walking, running, strafing and backing up relative to where they face, jumping (once per jump), sneaking,
+  swimming, attacks (wind-up on press, swing size by how long it was charged, chop/slash/thrust), spells, head and body tilt
+  following their aim, a death pose, and a "reading a book" pose while they have a menu open (their game is paused).
+  Attacks are animation only: an avatar never damages anything in your world.
+- **Parties (max 3):** shared party chat, vitals panel, and stand-ins for actors that are alive in a member's world but dead
+  or missing in yours (one per actor, never next to a living twin). **Kills are shared** (setting, on by default): if a member
+  kills an NPC or creature it dies for everybody in the group (essential NPCs excepted).
+- **Time and weather:** the host's clock and the weather in the host's region.
+- **Chat:** Enter or Y opens the input (the game keeps running); Tab switches Global/Party.
+
+### Commands
+`/players`, `/me text`, `/w name text`, `/r text`, `/g text`, `/p text`, `/goto name`, `/ip` (look up your address again),
+`/accept [name]`, `/decline [name]`, `/leave`, `/pkick name` (party leader).
+Host only: `/kick name`, `/ban name`, `/unban name`, `/mute name`, `/unmute name`, `/announce text`.
+
+### Testing
+`run-two.sh <openmw> <save.omwsave>` starts a host and a joiner (own user-data dirs, logs in `$TMPDIR/mp-two/`). The
+**Test: load a save with a test player** button on the multiplayer screen (or **Add a test player** in a running hosted game)
+puts a fake player next to you that accepts invites, chats, trades and shows vitals. `debug/` has helper scripts for the
+automated runs (auto-host, auto-join with a walking character, auto-bot, kill test).
+
+## Not done
+Shared fights where both worlds have the actor alive, container contents, stand-ins for actors that are alive but unloaded in
+your world, trade of enchanted/generated items, projectiles and spell effects of other players.
